# Bitwise golden vectors -- & | ^ and ~ over u64.
#
# EXTERNALLY AUTHORED ORACLE. Every expected value here was computed by a
# DIFFERENT implementation (Fable, test/data_bits_golden_vectors.json,
# 2026-08-21) and this file is GENERATED from that JSON. That matters more than
# usual: `&` and `|` are one character apart, both emit valid Zig, and both
# produce a number -- so a swapped operator is invisible to every compile-only
# gate in the tree (the BUG-226 class). An oracle we wrote ourselves could agree
# with our own bug; this one cannot.
#
# `~` is included as a POSITIVE CONTROL: it already worked (BUG-256), so if the
# not64 leg ever fails, the harness is broken rather than the new operators.
#
# Unsigned throughout because 8 of the 24 `a`/`b` values exceed i64 max.
# Shifts are deliberately NOT here -- they land with `<<`/`>>` in slice 2.

